    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s 2026-07-25 slate, the focus is squarely on exploiting the favorable matchup against Ryan Johnson, whose 4.89 xERA provides a significant ceiling for our top-tier plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** leads the charge with a 74.26 score, serving as our anchor despite the elite hold of the opposing battery. He is closely followed by **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52), both of whom benefit immensely from the wind-out conditions and favorable spots at the top of their respective orders. **Jonathan Aranda** and **Jeremiah Jackson** also emerge as primary targets, with **Aranda** projected for a high-efficiency outing against Tanner Bibee due to a strong dynamic platoon edge (+12%), and **Jeremiah Jackson** capitalizing on a massive park factor boost (+16%) at his home venue.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Bryce Harper**, who was ultimately relegated to the bench despite a 55.05 score. While **Bryce Harper** maintains a solid xwOBA of .384, the combination of a tough matchup against Ryan Weathers\u2019 3.46 xERA and a minor negative platoon shift (-13% SP skill impact) tipped the scale in favor of players like **Kyle Karros** and **Daulton Varsho**, who present more favorable situational leverage today. We are also keeping a close eye on the volatile \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board; should **Cal Raleigh** or **Yainer Diaz** drop down in their respective orders, their marginal scores (48.18 and 48.34, respectively) risk falling below the start threshold as we seek to protect our season-long game caps. Outside of these primary starters, we continue to monitor the availability of **Lawrence Butler** and **Tyler Freeman**, who remain on the periphery of our daily utility consideration should late lineup changes force a pivot.",
